    <article><a class="gimg" href="#"><img src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20300%20200%22%3E%3Crect%20width=%22300%22%20height=%22200%22%20fill=%22%23d9d9d9%22/%3E%3Ctext%20x=%22150%22%20y=%22105%22%20text-anchor=%22middle%22%20font-family=%22Inter,Arial,sans-serif%22%20font-size=%2213%22%20fill=%22%2369707d%22%3EPlaceholder%20image%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="Stanford’s AI Index Report 2026 meets the security reality in financial services"></a><div><h3 class="h24"><a href="#">Stanford’s AI Index Report 2026 meets the security reality in financial services</a></h3><p class="body16">AI is becoming core to financial services. But as adoption scales, so does risk. Without secure, real-time data, strong governance, and cyber resilience, AI can amplify threats as quickly as it drives innovation.</p><p class="gmeta">By<a href="#">Elastic</a></p></div></article>
